    <string name="key_app_info_title">App info for applying API keys</string>
    <string name="key_app_info_desc">AMap, Baidu and Google Android keys are bound to the package name plus the signing SHA1, so a key only works for apps installed with this signature. Copy the two values below when applying. Debug and release builds have different signatures and SHA1s; after changing the signature, add the new SHA1 in the console. Anyone you share the app with uses these same two values.</string>
    <string name="key_guide_title">How to apply for keys</string>
    <string name="key_guide_amap">1. Sign in at console.amap.com (personal developer verification is enough).\n2. App management → My apps → Create app, then Add Key.\n3. Choose the Android platform and enter the package name and SHA1 above (use this SHA1 for both release and debug codes).\n4. Paste the generated key into AMap API Key, save and restart the app.\nUsed for: map display, place search, route planning, location.</string>
    <string name="key_guide_baidu">1. At lbsyun.baidu.com open Console → App management → My apps → Create app.\n2. Choose Android SDK, enter the SHA1 (release) and package name above; the security code becomes SHA1;package.\n3. Paste the AK into Baidu Map API Key, save and restart the app.\nUsed for: map display, place search, route planning, and the real position indoors (returning after stopping, locating at startup).</string>
    <string name="key_guide_google">1. At console.cloud.google.com create a project and set up billing (there is a free allowance).\n2. Under APIs and Services enable Places API and Routes API.\n3. Credentials → Create credentials → API key; restrict it to Android apps and add the package name and SHA1 above.\n4. Paste the key into Google Maps API Key, save and restart the app.\nUsed for: place search and route planning. The Google map display key can only be set at build time.</string>
